@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] transfer-stream-custody-boundaries
Producer stdout MUST flow only to consumer stdin through a kernel pipe; disk
bytes never appear on helper stdout or become diagnostics. Diagnostics are
discarded with a 65536-byte cap. Deadline, excessive diagnostics, a failed
progress write or either failed child stop and reap both sides before exit.
Only two successful exits may return success. Only lilly-hostd runs this
helper, inside its command cgroup and under the stream lease it holds, with
argv it derived itself; cancellation is hostd killing that cgroup. A side
given a uid runs as that non-root uid with no supplementary groups and
no_new_privs. Byte rates are bounded integers using monotonic time with at
most 65536 bytes of burst credit; throttling never delays cancellation.
Progress is a fixed 8-byte counter overwritten at offset 0 of an inherited
regular file, at most once per second plus completion. Splice accounting is
transport progress only. No setuid or capabilities.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] transfer-stream-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the argv selector lattice against an independent
oracle, the credit-throttle arithmetic (refill matches a wide-arithmetic oracle,
credit stays within 0..=CREDIT_CAP_MS and the splice window never exceeds
credit/1000 bytes or SPLICE_WINDOW) and the side status mapping, while
process-level fixtures cover exact byte custody, adopted-descendant reaping,
deadline kills, diagnostics caps and the progress counter on an inherited
descriptor.
